  "body": "@\n## What changed\n\nThree units, one message from the user: (1) improve websearch analytics with ui-ux-pro-max, (2) make websearch request input/output readable, (3) stop pruning websearch content.\n\n**Measured problem:** the websearch analytics store capped each stored input/output JSON at 50k chars and replaced oversized payloads with a truncation envelope. On the live DB, **251 of 252 rows had truncated output** (avg 175k chars) — the dashboard detail view could not show what searches actually returned.\n\n### 1. Stop pruning websearch output (backend)\n`WEBSEARCH_LOG_CONTENT_MAX_CHARS` default raised **50,000 → 2,000,000** (~2 MB) across `settings.py`, `config/admin/websearch_manifest.py` (default `\"2000000\"`), and `.env.example`. The cap stays configurable as a safety valve; real provider output now always round-trips. Legacy truncated rows stay truncated (unrecoverable) but render the stored preview.\n\n### 2. Readable request input/output (frontend)\nThe websearch detail modal is reworked (flat+dense aesthetic preserved):\n- **Tool input** renders as a key/value summary (query, max results, domains) instead of raw JSON.\n- **Provider output** renders as readable per-result cards (title/url/published/snippet) with a **\"Show full content\"** toggle on long page text.\n- **Raw output JSON** moves to a collapsed `<details>` block with a **Copy** button — provider-specific fields stay inspectable without dumping 175k chars.\n- **Legacy truncated rows** show a notice + the stored preview + hash.\n- Reuses the existing `.turn-pane` / `.guide-copy-button` patterns.\n\n### 3. Fixed a pre-existing websearch export bug (found while verifying)\nThe websearch detail export mapped the `input`/`output`/`provider_config` fields to columns named literally `output` etc., which **do not exist** in `search_log` (the JSON lives in `input_json`/`output_json`/`provider_config_json`). Every websearch export selecting those fields failed with `no such column` and returned empty. `iter_export_rows` now aliases the `*_json` columns to the decoded names and `_attempt_dict` decodes either shape.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **Full-output storage test** (`test_full_output_is_stored_untruncated`): a ~60k-char output round-trips fully. **Confirmed to fail at the old 50k default** (§66 guard discipline).\n- **Export regression test** (`test_websearch_detail_export_carries_full_output`): decoded `output`/`input`/`provider_config` round-trip with full content. **Confirmed to fail without the alias fix** (OperationalError).\n- **jsdom harness** (real `admin.js` + `index.html`, §69): 24 assertions — input kv, readable cards, show-full toggle, raw JSON collapsed, copy buttons, legacy-truncated notice + auto-open.\n- **Live server on a throwaway home** (non-8082 port): `/admin/api/websearch/requests/1` returns full 60k output; export JSON carries it; server confirmed stopped after.\n- **Full suite**: 3713 passed, 16 pre-existing PS installer failures unchanged (documented baseline), 0 new regressions.\n- Static: `ruff format --check` clean, `ruff check` clean, `ty check` clean.\n\n## Versioning\n\nMINOR (new capability): **5.4.0 → 5.5.0**, `uv lock` regenerated in this commit.\n\n## Residual risks\n\n- **Legacy truncated rows stay truncated** (data already on disk). They render the stored preview + hash, so they are not blank.\n- **DB growth**: up to 2 MB per row if a content-extraction provider returns huge page text. Bounded by `WEBSEARCH_LOG_MAX_ROWS` (50k) and the operator can lower the cap or set `WEBSEARCH_LOG_CAPTURE_CONTENT=false`.\n- The main request-log `REQUEST_LOG_TEXT_MAX_CHARS` cap is untouched (out of scope).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n@",
