    "message": "feat(analytics): retain full websearch output (cap 50k -> 2M chars) + readable request detail\n\nThe websearch analytics store truncated every input/output payload over 50k\ncharacters into a {_truncated, preview, sha256} envelope. On the live DB,\n251 of 252 rows had truncated output (avg 175k chars) — so the dashboard\ndetail view could not show what most searches actually returned. The user\nasked to stop pruning websearch content.\n\n- Default WEBSEARCH_LOG_CONTENT_MAX_CHARS raised 50_000 -> 2_000_000\n  (settings, manifest default \"2000000\", .env.example); the configurable cap\n  stays as a safety valve, but real provider output now always round-trips.\n- Websearch detail modal reworked for readability: tool input renders as a\n  key/value summary, provider output as readable per-result cards with a\n  \"Show full content\" toggle on long page text, raw JSON moves to a collapsed\n  \"Raw output JSON\" details block with a Copy button, and legacy truncated\n  rows show a notice plus the stored preview. Reuses the turn-pane and\n  guide-copy-button patterns; flat+dense aesthetic unchanged.\n- Fixed a pre-existing websearch export bug: the detail export mapped the\n  \"input\"/\"output\"/\"provider_config\" fields to columns named literally\n  \"output\" etc., which do not exist in search_log (the JSON lives in *_json\n  columns), so every websearch export selecting those fields failed with\n  \"no such column\" and returned empty. iter_export_rows now aliases the *_json\n  columns to the decoded names and _attempt_dict decodes either shape.\n\nTests: full-output storage round-trip (fails at old 50k default), websearch\nexport carries full output (fails without the alias fix), settings/manifest\ndefault updates. 3713 passed, 16 pre-existing PS installer failures unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
